## Why This Is Asked
Tests streaming algorithm intuition and amortized reasoning. Detecting heavy hitters with bounded memory on a growing stream is a common interview topic; Misra–Gries provides deterministic guarantees with simple updates.

## Key Concepts
- Misra–Gries heavy-hitters
- Choice of k = floor(1/phi) + 1 to bound missed items
- Amortized O(1) per element, O(k) memory
- Trade-offs: larger k reduces false positives but uses more memory

## Code Example
```javascript
class MGHeavyHitters {
  constructor(k) {
    this.k = k;
    this.counters = new Map();
  }
  update(x) {
    if (this.counters.has(x)) {
      this.counters.set(x, this.counters.get(x) + 1);
      return;
    }
    if (this.counters.size < this.k) {
      this.counters.set(x, 1);
      return;
    }
    for (const [key, val] of Array.from(this.counters)) {
      if (val === 1) this.counters.delete(key);
      else this.counters.set(key, val - 1);
    }
  }
  candidates() { return Array.from(this.counters.keys()); }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate the phi-bound with a second pass or a secondary sketch in production?
- How does batch size B influence practical update throughput and memory usage?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests real-world streaming analytics: maintaining a dynamic feature (distinct count) under batched updates with tight per-batch guarantees. It probes data structures (circular buffers, counters), amortized reasoning, and practical optimizations under constrained space. 

## Key Concepts
- Sliding window maintenance
- Distinct counting with frequency map
- Amortized analysis under batched updates
- Space-conscious data structures and optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-implementation skeleton demonstrating the core idea
class WindowDistinct {
  constructor(W) {
    this.W = W;
    this.buf = new Array(W);
    this.freq = new Map();
    this.head = 0; // points to oldest element
    this.size = 0;
    this.distinct = 0;
  }
  init(arr) {
    for (let i = 0; i < this.W; i++) this.push(arr[i]);
  }
  push(x) {
    if (this.size < this.W) this.size++;
    else {
      this.pop();
    }
    this.buf[this.head] = x;
    this.head = (this.head + 1) % this.W;
    const c = (this.freq.get(x) || 0) + 1;
    this.freq.set(x, c);
    if (c === 1) this.distinct++;
  }
  pop() {
    const idx = (this.head) % this.W;
    const y = this.buf[idx];
    const c = this.freq.get(y) - 1;
    if (c === 0) this.freq.delete(y);
    else this.freq.set(y, c);
    if (c === 0) this.distinct--;
  }
  batchUpdate(batch) {
    for (const x of batch) this.push(x);
  }
  query() {
    return this.distinct;
  }
}
```

